WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:01.270
Last time on...

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.560
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.600
--...<i>zura</i>!
--Aqours had to perform

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.360
both in the school open house
and Love Live on the same day.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.480
Eternal life... Phoenix!

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.820
So, where's our school?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.110
It's over here, but there's no bus or train
that goes all the way there, so...

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.780
We did all we could to perform
in both concerts, but...

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.750
Hey, girls. Wanna lift?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.790
We were going to fail until
some friends gave us a huge hand, <i>zura</i>!

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.470
And so, both of our concerts
were a huge success.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.180
--Morning!
--Huh?

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.800
I'm off! I'll see you at school!

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.180
You're quite early!

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.520
Morning, Shiitake!
Mito-<i>nee</i>! Shima-<i>nee</i>! See you later!

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.270
She's early!

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.280
I wonder if it's going to rain today.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.030
She's in a pretty good mood.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.570
She is, at a time like this...

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.620
Maybe she's forgotten...

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.910
I think that's very possible.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.460
Really?

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:05.290
Chika-<i>chan</i>.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.370
Yeah?

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.210
Do you remember what today is?

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.280
Hmm...

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.170
The day they announce the results
of the Love Live qualifiers, right?

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.430
--Whoa!
--She remembers, <i>zura</i>!

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.050
A-Aren't you nervous?

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.760
Not at all!

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:24.270
It went very well and we were able
to sing such a wonderful song.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.270
We definitely passed it!

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.850
When I talked to Sarah-<i>san</i> yesterday...

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.190
As far as I can tell, you won't just pass,
you'll probably be the top-ranked group.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.480
--You really think so?!
--Whoa!

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.000
So she said.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.530
Really?

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:39.110
When did you two get so close?

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.740
It's here!

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.950
"Love Live Qualifiers Results"

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.620
Gulp.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.620
I'm so nervous, <i>zura</i>.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:49.880
H-Here we go!

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:51.380
"Love Live Qualifiers Results"

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.250
"Aqours Has Passed Qualifiers"

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.820
Is it possible that this means
we were the top-ranked group?

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.800
--I told you!
--We did it, <i>zura</i>!

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.470
Yes, do as you wish.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.140
Mari!

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.140
Wooooo...

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.010
Oh, yes!

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.430
--You, too, Dia-<i>san</i>!
--What?

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.020
Yeah...

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:28.250
<i>Let's throw our all at each other</i>
<i>and grab hold of the future!</i>

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:38.880
<i>The sky and this ocean are both on our side</i>

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.850
<i>Shining and saying, "Go, do your best!"</i>

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:49.560
<i>To let our voices reach far, far away</i>

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:54.480
<i>Shall we shout our dreams louder?</i>

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.230
<i>(Full of hope)</i>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:03:00.570
<i>Today pulls tomorrow toward itself</i>

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:09.160
<i>It's really fun to grasp the magnet</i>
<i>in my heart and run right now!</i>

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.290
<i>(Let's always go together)</i>

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.080
<i>What shall we do about the future?!</i>

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:21.880
<i>Everyone laughs and cries</i>
<i>as</i> <i>they</i> <i>look for the shape of their dreams</i>

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:30.310
<i>Because I'm sure the</i> <i>future</i> <i>us</i>
<i>will have the answer</i>

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:38.400
<i>Let's run with everything we have</i>
<i>and become the shining wind</i>

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.740
<i>We got dream</i>

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.160
That being said...

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.980
"#4 'Don't Be So Formal with Me'"

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.350
Again?

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.790
What is it this time?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.960
Well, we performed in two events,
the school open house and Love Live, right?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.960
So, we're broke.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.210
We put in a thousand yen each the other day.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.630
It's already gone?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.720
As it stands, we'll run out of money...

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.180
And even if we could go to the final round...

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.850
Everyone! We're setting sail for Tokyo!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.770
Yeah!

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.370
...we'll end up like that, <i>zura</i>.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.350
We'll sink!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.610
How much do we have left?

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.910
Wow! Such a pretty coin!

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.070
F-F-F...

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:26.940
Five yen?!

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.600
Maybe it's a good luck coin...

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.810
I'm so happy!

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.270
This is no time for goofing around!

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.450
What's wrong?

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:36.500
Ah... Nothing. I just thought that
both Kanan-<i>san</i> and Mari-<i>san</i>

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.630
have gotten closer to the others.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.760
What do you think, Kanan-<i>chan</i>, <i>zura</i>?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.720
Well...

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.450
Kanan... -<i>chan</i>...?

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.350
So... you suddenly turn to the gods for help?

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.310
I wonder if they'll grant our wish...

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.350
Please increase our five yen
five-fold... or ten-fold...

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.900
No, a hundred-fold!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.980
That'll still only be five hundred yen.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:01.610
Ah...

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.070
Hm?! What is this spiritual pressure I sense?!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.110
There's nothing here, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.830
Wait, you have the third eye?

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.910
Well, instead of turning
to the divine, can't we just...

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.830
Mari-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.170
We can't ask my family for help!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.590
Yeah, I figured...

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.920
Mari... -<i>chan</i>...?

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.930
See you tomorrow, Mari-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.640
Kanan-<i>chan</i>! I'll bring the book
with me tomorrow!

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:30.430
Okay!

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.370
Sis! Come on!

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.520
So, what did you want to talk to us about?

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:41.270
What? Well, it's nothing
important, but... uhm...

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.990
It's just that it didn't take you two
long to get all buddy-buddy...

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.110
Buddy-buddy?

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.240
Me and Kanan?

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:54.240
No, I meant with the first
and second-year students!

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.290
Huh?

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.750
Wait, don't tell me... Are you jealous, Dia?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.840
N-No way! It's just that
I cannot set a good example

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:07.420
unless I duly follow the rules
as the student council president.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.840
Here you go again. You're always so obstinate.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.470
Very hard-headed, aren't you?

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.390
I just...

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.060
--You just...?
--You just...?

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.170
I just...

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:27.180
Nothing! But do always remember
that you two are their upperclassmen.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.200
What do you think?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.330
It smells big time. The fires of jealousy!

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.040
I'm sure she'll show her true self soon enough,

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:44.500
since Dia can be a bit of a dunderhead
when it comes to her own feelings.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.160
Dunderhead?

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:52.420
Mari-<i>chan</i>... Kanan-<i>chan</i>... Hmm...

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.890
Part-time job?

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.890
Yeah, we don't have much choice.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:06:59.890
Oh?

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.770
What is it this time?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.080
Ah, yes?

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.610
Does your stomach hurt?

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.480
No!

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.530
W-Well, I thought you were
looking at something.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.410
Yes. We're looking for work
in Uchiura. We thought

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.780
a job at a convenience store
or delivering papers might be good.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:20.000
Then Numazu may be
a better place to look for work.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:23.210
"Part-time Jobs"

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.710
Numazu, huh?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.210
There are tons of different jobs in Numazu.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.540
Like café jobs!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.340
Welcome! How many in your party?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.920
Flower shops!

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:33.680
Yes, this flower is
the prettiest one we have right now!

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.600
If you're looking for something different,
you can be a model for a photo studio.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.430
Say "Cheese"!

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:44.730
"Part-time Jobs"

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.900
Wow, that sounds kinda fun!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:43.780
Right?

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:45.730
We'll work in Numazu. It's now decided!

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:51.070
Bzzzzt! You're thinking too simple!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.410
Working isn't so easy! In addition,

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.120
work shifts are usually four days a week
or more, including on weekends,

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.410
so it'll be hard for the nine of us
to practice together!

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.790
Besides, you shouldn't decide things so easily!

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.750
Think things through!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:08.590
Ah...

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:11.260
Dia-<i>san</i> is certainly right.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.760
That's our Dia-<i>san</i>!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.590
But what're we gonna do then?

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.010
Can you think of something, Dia-<i>san</i>?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.100
W-Well...

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.930
"Numazu Flea Market"
"Central Park"

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.930
Flea market, huh?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.270
This way, we can earn some money
without losing too much time!

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.070
This is great, sis!

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:31.110
So Dia-<i>san</i> can come up
with an idea like this, too, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.780
You're so cool, Dia-<i>san</i>!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.950
W-Well, I wouldn't really...

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.490
...disagree with you!

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:40.200
I shall bestow this
fallen angel's feather upon you.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.620
I feel honored.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:45.580
All right! Now, if I can get
closer to them and gain their trust...

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:50.880
Let's go home together... Dia-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:55.510
Let's read these, <i>zura</i>... Dia-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:55.510 --> 00:09:00.930
Here you go. It's the picture
from the other day, Dia-<i>chan</i>!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.080
D-Dia?

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.370
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:10.480
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.980
That costume...

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.160
Mito-<i>nee</i> said that her company
won't be using it anymore, so...

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.660
What do you think?

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.450
What exactly are you trying to accomplish?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.580
Mandarin orange lady!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.910
Hi! I'm a mandarin orange! You should
eat mandarin oranges in winter.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:29.130
--Go! Vitamin C power!
--Jeez...

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.050
How much is this?

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.920
Hm? How much should I charge...?

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.340
But... this is all I have.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.220
Well...

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.980
Thank you!

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.350
Thanks for coming!

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.060
All right! Our money got doubled!

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.760
It's thanks to Benzaiten-<i>sama</i>.

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:50.780
Yep!

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:52.860
What are you saying?

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:53.680
Huh?

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:54.990
Think things through.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:59.280
We're here to make money
to fund Aqours' activities, remember?

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.990
We need to steel ourselves
so that we can make money!

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.450
But...

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.940
Excuse me. Is one thousand yen okay for this?

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:07.920
Just watch!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.120
What?

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.330
Welcome!

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.750
Unfortunately, considering how much
it originally cost,

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.590
I have to say bzzzzt to going any lower!

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:15.670
B-But...

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:19.680
Frankly speaking, although this isn't
brand new, it's never been used!

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:23.610
To sell these items, we cleaned them
with care one by one.

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:24.850
These are our treasures!

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:29.060
And yet, look at these prices!
We're already practically giving them away!

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.820
You shouldn't point your finger at customers.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.490
We have to ride a swan boat to Tokyo, <i>zura</i>.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.370
--What?!
--At any rate...

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:44.450
That was some pretty firm
determination on display earlier, huh?

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:45.950
"Central Park"

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:45.950
Just as you'd expect from Dia-<i>san</i>!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.120
Yeah.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:52.130
Compared to that, I can't believe
you brought something like that, Mari.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.090
Were you planning to sell it?

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:58.170
In that regard, Yoshiko also sold nothing!

00:10:58.510 --> 00:10:59.810
It's Yohane.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:07.850
It's as if they're
healing the wounds in my heart...

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.350
Such a beautiful scene...

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.730
Stop talking nonsense!
Hurry up and pick them up already!

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.190
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.290
Q-Quick, everyone!

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:20.820
"Central Park"

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.860
Kanan-<i>chan</i>...

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.620
Did something happen to Dia-<i>san</i>?

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:28.930
Why?

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:30.580
Just a hunch...

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:35.500
It's funny how you have
a good nose for things like that.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.670
Ah... Is that a compliment?

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.470
It is. Don't worry about her.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:44.010
Mari and I will take care of it.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:48.100
"Ootemachi"
"Numazu Tozan Tokai Bus"
 "Izuhakone"

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.470
Well then, we're going ahead.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.100
Be careful.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.520
So, what is it that
you want to talk to me about?

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.360
Can't it wait till tomorrow?

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.480
You're hiding something
after all, aren't you, Dia?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.530
If you want to be close to the lowerclassmen,

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.740
you should just tell them so.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.410
That's not the case! It's not like...

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.740
--What do you think?
--She's guilty!

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:09.700
What?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.040
When you try to hide something,

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:14.120
you always start scratching
the area around your mole.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.800
I-It's nothing!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.420
You can't get away now.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.490
Now, tell us!

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:31.020
Well... I just...

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:32.140
--You just...?
--I just...

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.270
Promise you won't laugh?

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.390
Laugh?

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:39.780
There's no way we'll do that!

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:40.920
But...

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.070
Oh, jeez...

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.950
How long do you think
we've known each other?!

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.020
Fine, I'll tell you.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.990
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.340
At any rate, to think that...

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:08.010
Dia wants to be called Dia-<i>chan</i>...

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:13.270
It's not like I want to be called that.
I told you so many times, didn't I?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.020
But no one else gets called with "-<i>san</i>."

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.060
That's no big deal.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:22.150
It is! Having a distance
between members like this

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:25.280
kind of, sort of is not
a good thing moving forward.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.910
So, you're jealous.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:30.910
I am not!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.080
Just as we'd expect from our Dia!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:36.340
More importantly,
why did you ask me to come here?

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.330
Okay, everyone! Let's behave today!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.080
Okay, everyone! Let's behave today!

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:39.290
Oh, I see. You haven't heard, huh?

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.920
Okay!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.670
We got a message from You.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:45.850
She wants us to help out
at this event, at least for today.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:45.880
Now everyone, don't fall behind.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:46.930
Where?

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:47.590
Here.

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:49.300
Here?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.240
We'll work together all day today.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.680
So, this is a chance for you to get closer
to them and be called Dia-<i>chan</i>.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.190
Dia... -<i>chan</i>...

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:09.660
"Welcome to sea paradise"
"Izu-Mito Sea Paradise"

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:05.820
I-It's not like I want that, so...

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.070
You say that, but...

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.660
It's totally written all over your face.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:19.250
Dolphins are amazing!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.090
Well then, are you guys ready to work?

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.380
Hm? You-<i>chan</i>?

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.360
Where are you?

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.510
I'm right here!

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:28.550
Whoa! When did you...?

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:31.140
As a first step, we split up
into groups of three.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.810
Yeah!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:42.440
"Popcorn" "Sausages"
"Take-out Shop"

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.720
You-<i>san</i> seems quite familiar with this work.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.730
She said she's worked here before.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.440
Now, you won't be able to
get closer to them if you are with us.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.270
Hey! Hurry up! Come on!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.280
O-Okay.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:49.700
Here's your udon with fried tofu!
Thank you for waiting!

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.950
"Pick up food here"

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.950
Thank you.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.780
Another order of udon, please!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:54.870
I don't do well with noodles, <i>zura</i>.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.580
Hey! We don't have time to relax!

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.120
--<i>Zura</i>...
--Okay.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.000
Oh, that's right!

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:04.250
Like I said the other day,
you're so obstinate, Dia.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:07.050
Just start off with some small talk...

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.290
Small talk...

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.970
Ch-Chika-<i>san</i>.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.050
Yes?

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:16.930
I-It's a fine day today, isn't it?

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.980
Y-Yeah...

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:23.560
Hanamaru-<i>san</i>, you don't like udon?

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.520
What's going on?
Did something happen?

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:26.480
Did it, <i>zura</i>?

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:30.110
I don't know, <i>zura</i>...
But it looks like she's probably...

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:35.660
--...super upset, <i>zura</i>!
--...super upset, <i>zura</i>!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.790
To think that I looked upset...

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:44.500
I can't seem to get it right.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.750
Dia-<i>san</i>!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:48.200
You don't have to work at the shop, sis?

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:56.180
"Izu-Mito Sea Paradise"

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:52.130
Yeah, since less people come to the shop
now that lunch time is over,

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.380
I came here to give them a hand.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:56.180
What is that?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.220
It's the food for the sea lion.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:01.390
We borrowed a training whistle
from the trainer, too.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.330
That's good.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.610
Oh, hello, sea lion.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.740
He's saying that he wants food.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.950
But looking at a sea lion close up...

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:19.630
He's bigger than we thought. In addition...

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.040
...he's got dog-like... whiskers.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.380
Higher ground! We need
to reach higher ground right now!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.800
The whistle... The whistle...!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.300
Ruby-<i>chan</i>! Get a move on!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.100
This isn't good!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.260
Hurry up or he'll eat you!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.640
The sea lion is right behind you! Ruby-<i>chan</i>!

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:41.890
--Be quiet!
--I'm scared!

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.450
Go back to the pool!

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:47.400
That was incredible...

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.980
Just as you'd expect from my sis...

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.370
Phew...

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:56.950
Hey! This isn't good. If I keep up like this,
they'll think I'm obstinate again.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.080
Things aren't going well?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.710
Well, I didn't think they would, though.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.040
Why?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.960
You're not really the outgoing type.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:12.800
Ever since elementary school,
you've always just hung out with us.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:14.590
I-It wasn't like that...

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:17.090
Nothing will change unless <i>you</i> go to them.

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.050
Even so...

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.140
What should I do?

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.310
It's easy. First...

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:26.230
Y-You... -<i>chan</i>...

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:29.820
"Aquarium Entrance"

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.970
Yohane! Descend!

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:29.820
Hm...? Did you say something, Dia-<i>san</i>?

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:31.440
--Well...
--I want one!

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:34.150
"Tickets"
"Adults - 2,200 yen" "Children - 1,100 yen"

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:32.510
Uhm...

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:34.150
Would you like to hand these out, too?

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.160
Thank you... You-<i>chan</i>...

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:46.280
Let's work hard together, Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:48.710
It's Yohane.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:49.790
Seriously?!

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.710
"Uchicchi"

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:54.880
No? But I just felt a chill
go down my spine. Something is amiss.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.010
I get what you're saying.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:18:00.180
It's as if a messenger from the celestial sphere
has materialized a new world...

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:01.970
Okay, I lost you there.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:05.520
"Pick up food here"

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.520
Dia-<i>san</i> was upset, <i>zura</i>.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.190
Yeah...

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.810
Hey, aren't there too many bubbles?

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:12.150
I put all the detergent in so that
they'll get cleaned sooner, <i>zura</i>.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.400
Wow! Good thinking!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:14.800
<i>Zura</i>.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.420
--Ah!
--Ah!

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.040
Be careful, both of you.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.250
--Yes, ma'am.
--Yes, ma'am.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.750
My sister is acting strange?

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:33.000
She somehow seemed very upset.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.920
She looked distressed.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.010
I bet something really did happen.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:38.220
How naïve.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.800
That's the smile of someone
who has been imbued with darkness.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:41.800
"Uchicchi"

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.970
Well, it could be that... or something else.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:46.350
What should we do?

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:49.940
We probably shouldn't leave them
in the dark any longer.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:53.360
Dia... -<i>chan</i>...?

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:59.030
I think she wants to get closer to you guys.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:00.160
That's why...

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.990
Then that smile didn't mean
that she was upset, <i>zura</i>?

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:07.290
In any case, I didn't know
Dia-<i>san</i> had a cute side like this.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:08.910
She should've just told us.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.290
Right?

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.710
That's why Kanan and I are the only ones

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.590
who've seen that side of her
since elementary school.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:20.550
She's serious, well-behaved, smart,
and speaks in a formal manner.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:25.470
She's dependable,
but we somehow feel she's above us.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:29.560
Because everyone felt that way,
Dia also thought she should act like it.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.520
So, she distanced herself
from others more and more.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:35.800
When the truth is,
she tends to get lonely easily.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:45.990
"Discovery Exhibition"
"Ticket Office"

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.990
Hey! Wait!

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:49.870
Seriously, everyone! Behave yourselves!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.870
Mr. Sea Lion!

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.670
Whoa! What's going on?!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.130
Oh, no!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.140
Hey, don't run!

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:06.390
Oh, no... They aren't listening to us at all.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:09.790
Hey!

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:17.780
What?!

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:17.780
♪ You made them cry. You made them cry. ♪

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.730
What?!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.730
♪ You made them cry. You made them cry. ♪

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:19.650
What do we do?

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.880
Things have gotten out of hand.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.440
Behave yourselves...

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:34.580
Now, everyone! Come to the stadium!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:42.880
Kindergarteners! If you run or yell,
it'll cause trouble for others.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.010
That's a definite bzzzzt!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.760
So behave yourselves, okay?

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.010
Okay!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:10.150
In the end, I guess I am who I am, huh?

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.160
I think that's how it should be.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:17.600
I want you to be who you are, Dia-<i>san</i>.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.050
It's true that unlike Kanan-<i>chan</i> and Mari-<i>chan</i>,

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:26.450
I sometimes feel that
I can't fool around or joke with you.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:31.430
But when push comes to shove,
you've always got our backs.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:34.850
When we slack off, you scold us.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.700
You keep us on track!

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:43.340
That makes us all feel better, too.
So, we love you just how you are, Dia-<i>san</i>!

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.360
Right, everyone?

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:49.740
So, please continue to be our Dia-<i>san</i>!

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:52.040
Please continue to keep us in line!

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:02.050
I don't really care how you refer to me.

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:08.800
One, two...

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:10.520
Dia-<i>chan</i>!

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:18.150
<i>Try and be brave</i>

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:20.690
<i>I know it's actually scary</i>

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:26.700
<i>It's not like I was able</i>
<i>to</i> <i>do it from the start, either</i>

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:29.530
<i>I messed up a lot</i>

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:32.200
<i>I was really frustrated</i>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:37.750
<i>But</i> <i>that</i> <i>gave</i> <i>me</i> <i>strength,</i>
<i>so</i> <i>just</i> <i>don't</i> <i>give</i> <i>up</i>

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:43.460
<i>Tears</i> <i>in</i> <i>your</i> <i>eyes</i>
<i>that</i> <i>want</i> <i>to</i> <i>try</i> <i>believing</i>

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:47.720
<i>Say "bye-bye" to hesitation and tears</i>

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:49.390
<i>Now, let's go!</i>

00:22:49.390 --> 00:22:54.560
<i>Let's chase them as</i> <i>many</i> <i>times</i>
<i>as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:57.810
<i>Everyone fails sometimes</i>

00:22:57.810 --> 00:23:00.850
<i>But dreams won't fade, dreams won't fade</i>

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:06.240
<i>Let's chase them as</i> <i>many</i> <i>times</i>
<i>as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:14.280
<i>'Cause today is today, and once</i>
<i>you</i> <i>wake up, it'll be a new morning</i>

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:22.290
<i>Oh, the sun's smiling down on you</i>

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:41.460
"#5 'Taking in A Dog'"

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:38.730
Next Time! "Taking in a Dog."
